  "prefLabel": "Home 403.06 Waiver of Continuing Education Deadline",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Home 403.06 Waiver of Continuing Education Deadline. A waiver of continuing education deadlines shall be granted provided that a petition to that effect is filed at least 30 days before the expiration of the biennial renewal period in question or that late filing is justified by a showing of good cause. Good cause shall include accident, illness, or other circumstances beyond the control of the licensee. No waiver petition shall be granted which does not propose a specific timetable for completing specific courses which will meet the petitioner’s continuing education deficiency.\n\nSource. #9506, eff 7-8-09; ss by #12463, eff 1-23-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/home100-600.html"
